# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in this project should ever need a key at build or run time (the game
# is a single static file with no server), but a stray .env is the single most
# common way a key reaches a public repo — so it is blocked outright.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `build-itch.sh` writes here. Never commit it: it is generated, and committing
# it makes it easy to accidentally ship whatever happens to be lying in the dir.
/dist/
*.zip

# ── Local noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
